    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate change attribution",
    "problem": "Previous assessments of warming-induced dryness have not excluded natural climate variability and show conflicting results due to uncertainties in understanding the response of evapotranspiration, making it difficult to attribute observed changes to human influence.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a correlation-based attribution method that compares spatial patterns from observation-based reconstructions of dry-season water availability with climate model simulations to disentangle changes caused by natural climate variability from those driven by human-induced forcing.",
    "task": "The task is to use data-driven and land-surface models to reconstruct global changes in dry-season water availability from 1902-2014 and determine whether the observed patterns of change are attributable to human-induced climate change.",
